# Jaspr Web Development Guide

## Core Mission
Expert Jaspr development assistant for modern, SEO-friendly websites using Dart. Leverage Flutter knowledge while mastering Jaspr-specific patterns.

## When to Use Jaspr
**✅ RECOMMEND for:**
- SEO-critical sites (marketing, blogs, docs)
- Server-side rendering (SSR) or static generation (SSG)
- Multi-page applications with fast loading
- Dart-first web development

**❌ AVOID for:**
- Mobile apps (use Flutter)
- Heavy client-side interactions (consider Flutter Web)
- JavaScript ecosystem dependencies

## Quick Setup
```bash
dart --version  # Requires >=3.0
dart pub global activate jaspr_cli
jaspr create my_project
cd my_project && jaspr serve
```

## Project Architecture
```
lib/
├── main.dart           # Entry point
├── app.dart            # Root component + routing
├── router.dart         # Route definitions
├── envs.dart           # Environment variables
├── core/               # Utilities & abstractions
├── data_*/             # Data layer (models, APIs, resources)
├── di/                 # Dependency injection
└── {feature}/          # Feature-specific UI components
```

## Component Patterns

### Basic Component Structure
```dart
class MyComponent extends StatelessComponent {
  const MyComponent({required this.data, super.key});
  final DataType data;

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield div(classes: ['container'], [
      // Semantic HTML structure
    ]);
  }
}
```

### Semantic HTML Priority
```dart
// ✅ GOOD - Semantic structure
yield main([
  header([nav([/* navigation */])]),
  section([
    h1([text('Page Title')]),
    article([/* content */]),
  ]),
  footer([/* footer content */]),
]);
```

## Styling Strategy

### Native CSS (Recommended)
Use Jaspr's type-safe CSS system with `@css` annotations:

```dart
@css
final styles = [
  css('.hero')
    .background(color: Color(0xFF1a1a1a))
    .padding(Padding.symmetric(vertical: 4.rem, horizontal: 2.rem))
    .text(
      color: Colors.white,
      fontSize: 3.rem,
      fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
      lineHeight: 1.2.rem,
    ),
  
  css('.card')
    .background(color: Colors.white)
    .border(Border.all(color: Color(0xFFe5e7eb), width: 1.px))
    .borderRadius(BorderRadius.circular(0.5.rem))
    .padding(Padding.all(1.5.rem))
    .boxShadow(BoxShadow(
      color: Color(0x1A000000),
      offset: Offset(0.px, 4.px),
      blurRadius: 6.px,
    )),

  // Responsive design
  css.media(MediaQuery.screen(minWidth: 768.px), [
    css('.hero').fontSize(4.rem),
    css('.grid').display(Display.grid).gridTemplate(
      columns: GridTracks([
        GridTrack.fr(1),
        GridTrack.fr(1),
      ]),
    ),
  ]),
];
```

### Key CSS API Patterns
```dart
// Colors - Use Color() constructor, not Color.hex()
.color(Color(0xFF1a1a1a))

// Spacing - Use .only(), .symmetric(), .all()
.margin(Margin.only(top: 2.rem, bottom: 1.rem))
.padding(Padding.symmetric(horizontal: 1.5.rem))

// Position - Parameters for absolute/relative
.position(Position.absolute(top: 0.px, left: 0.px))

// Grid - Use GridTemplate with GridTracks
.gridTemplate(columns: GridTracks([
  GridTrack.fr(1),
  GridTrack.minmax(TrackSize.px(200), TrackSize.fr(1)),
]))

// Units - Use extension methods
2.rem, 16.px, 100.percent, 50.vh

// Transitions
.transition(Transition(
  property: 'all',
  duration: Duration(milliseconds: 300),
  timingFunction: TimingFunction.ease,
))
```

## Routing Setup
```dart
// lib/app.dart
class App extends StatelessComponent {
  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    yield Router(routes: [
      Route(path: '/', builder: (_, __) => HomePage()),
      Route(path: '/about', builder: (_, __) => AboutPage()),
      Route(path: '/blog/:slug', builder: (context, state) {
        final slug = state.pathParameters['slug']!;
        return BlogPostPage(slug: slug);
      }),
    ]);
  }
}
```

## Data Patterns

### Server-Side (SEO-friendly)
```dart
class BlogPage extends StatelessComponent {
  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    final posts = await ApiService.fetchPosts(); // Server-rendered
    yield div([
      ...posts.map((post) => PostCard(post: post)),
    ]);
  }
}
```

### Client-Side (Interactive)
```dart
class DynamicContent extends StatefulComponent {
  @override
  State<DynamicContent> createState() => _DynamicContentState();
}

class _DynamicContentState extends State<DynamicContent> {
  List<Item> items = [];
  bool isLoading = true;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    _loadData();
  }

  Future<void> _loadData() async {
    try {
      final data = await ApiService.fetchUserData();
      setState(() {
        items = data;
        isLoading = false;
      });
    } catch (e) {
      setState(() {
        isLoading = false;
        // Handle error appropriately
      });
    }
  }

  @override
  Iterable<Component> build(BuildContext context) sync* {
    if (isLoading) {
      yield div(classes: ['loading'], [text('Loading...')]);
      return;
    }

    yield div([
      ...items.map((item) => ItemCard(item: item)),
    ]);
  }
}
```

